---
import Base from '../../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import AdSlot from '../../../../components/AdSlot.astro';
import {estrofasDeCanto} from '../../../../lib/corpus';
const selections=[1144,1145,1146];
const sections=[{"heading":"A father and a friend","body":"The first stanza presents counsel as an offer of companionship rather than command. The speaker claims the authority of experience, but he also acknowledges the fear that danger can be hidden nearby. A reader can value the invitation to trust while noticing the defensiveness that years of conflict have produced."},{"heading":"Admitting that a life can teach imperfectly","body":"The next stanza admits that Fierro has learned through misfortune and may still be mistaken. His capacity to advise is therefore not proof that he has behaved without fault. That admission gives the relationship more human depth."},{"heading":"Learning what is worth knowing","body":"The distinction between learning much and learning good things asks what education is for. It is not an argument against knowledge: the speaker is asking what kinds of knowledge guide action well. The colloquial spellings belong to the original literary voice."},{"heading":"A question for present-day families","body":"Can parents offer guidance while remaining open about their own errors? This is a contemporary reflection prompted by the poem, not a timeless rule that Hernández explicitly established for all families."}];
const stanzas=estrofasDeCanto('vuelta',32).filter(s=>selections.includes(s.numero));
---
<Base lang="en-US" adKind="article" pageType="Article" title="A Father Who Gives Advice Is More Than a Father: Martín Fierro Explained" description="Read the original verses beginning 'Un padre que da consejos' and an English interpretation of fatherhood, friendship, caution and family in Martín Fierro.">
<article class="study"><nav class="crumb"><a href="/en/">English home</a> / <a href="/en/library/">Popular library</a> / <a href="/en/martin-fierro-advice-to-his-sons/">Advice to his sons</a></nav><header><p class="eyebrow">FATHERHOOD · FAMILY · WISDOM · ORIGINAL SPANISH VERSES</p><h1>A Father Who Gives Advice Is More Than a Father: Martín Fierro Explained</h1><p class="intro">The first words of Fierro’s advice join two roles: a father and a friend. Yet the next lines turn to danger, uncertainty and the lessons of a hard life. The result is tender without being sentimental.</p></header><figure><img src="/media/fotografias-v3/consejos-fogon-hijos.webp" alt="Modern illustrated reconstruction of Martín Fierro giving counsel to three young men around a campfire"/><figcaption>Contemporary editorial illustration; not an archival document.</figcaption></figure><div class="reading"><section><h2>The original verses, Canto XXXII (1879)</h2><p>These selected stanzas are drawn directly from the site's original Spanish corpus; editorial explanation follows separately.</p>{stanzas.map(s=><section class="stanza" lang="es"><h3>Estrofa {s.numero}</h3><blockquote>{s.versos.map(v=><span>{v.texto}</span>)}</blockquote><a href={`/en/martin-fierro-advice-to-his-sons/#${s.id}`} lang="en">See the stanza in the complete canto</a></section>)}</section><AdSlot id="article-02-after-original-verses" kind="article"/><section><h2>Reading the poem with care</h2>{sections.map((s,i)=><><section><h3>{s.heading}</h3><p>{s.body}</p></section>{i===1&&<AdSlot id="article-03-mid-commentary" kind="article"/>}{i===2&&<AdSlot id="article-04-late-commentary" kind="article"/>}</>)}</section><section class="sources"><h2>Original text and reading companions</h2><p>José Hernández, <em>La vuelta de Martín Fierro</em> (1879), Canto XXXII. The quotations are read from the same repository corpus as the Spanish reader. This article is original English interpretation, not a translation or a claim about Hernández's personal beliefs.</p><p><a href="/leer/vuelta/32/" lang="es">Read the complete original canto</a> · <a href="/en/martin-fierro-advice-to-his-sons/">All 31 stanzas with commentary</a> · <a href="/en/library/themes-and-analysis/">Literary analysis</a></p></section><AdSlot id="article-05-end" kind="article"/></div></article>
